# PHP Deserialization - Arbitrary File Deletion via Object Injection

## Executive Summary

A PHP deserialization vulnerability was identified in the application's session management mechanism. The application stores a serialized PHP object inside a client-controlled cookie and later deserializes it without validating its integrity.

By modifying the `avatar_link` property of the serialized object, it is possible to force the server to delete an arbitrary file instead of the authenticated user's avatar during the account deletion process.

This allows an attacker to delete files accessible by the web server, resulting in arbitrary file deletion.

