# Summary

The application stores user information inside a serialized PHP object contained in the session cookie.

One of the serialized properties, `avatar_link`, specifies the location of the user's avatar file.

When the user deletes their account, the server deserializes the cookie and blindly passes the value of `avatar_link` to a file deletion function.

Since the serialized object is entirely controlled by the client and lacks integrity protection, an attacker can modify the file path to point to any file on the server.

