# Key Takeaways

- Client-controlled serialized objects must never be trusted.
- Deserialized properties should never be used directly in filesystem operations.
- File paths should always be generated and validated server-side.
- Insecure deserialization can lead to arbitrary file deletion, privilege escalation, or even remote code execution depending on the application's logic.
